<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">III-C</span> </span><span id="S3.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Parameter spaces and function properties </span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We next provide a theoretical analysis showing why inserting more Adapter blocks (or changing them)
can increase the capacity of the model in a supremum sense,
yet might not guarantee better actual performance under different insert settings.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the parameter space of the pre-trained encoder without adapters, then the model is <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{0}(x)\in\Theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{0}(x)\in\Theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{N,loc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{N,loc}</annotation></semantics></math> be the parameter space when we insert <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> adapter blocks at certain positions <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="loc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">loc</annotation></semantics></math>.
A performance measure is</p>
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\bigl(x,\,\theta,\,N,\,loc\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\bigl(x,\,\theta,\,N,\,loc\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta_{N,loc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta_{N,loc}</annotation></semantics></math> includes both original pre-trained parameters (often frozen) and newly introduced parameters of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> adapters. We write</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}}}f(\theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>loc</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}}}f(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">for the maximum achievable performance in that space, and <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\theta^{*}(\Theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>loc</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\theta^{*}(\Theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}}))</annotation></semantics></math> for the actual solution found by a given adapter location <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="loc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">loc</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we propose two theorems and put proof session at Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Additional theorem proof ‣ A Simple Efficiency Incremental Learning Framework via Vision-Language Model with Nonlinear Multi-Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Monotonic Bound on Performance)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{0}\;\subseteq\;\Theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}}\;\subseteq\;\Theta_{M,\mathrm{loc}},\quad M&gt;N\geq 0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>loc</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">⊆</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>loc</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{0}\;\subseteq\;\Theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}}\;\subseteq\;\Theta_{M,\mathrm{loc}},\quad M&gt;N\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then</span><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E9X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{M,\mathrm{loc}}}f(x,\theta,M,\mathrm{loc})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>loc</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>loc</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{M,\mathrm{loc}}}f(x,\theta,M,\mathrm{loc})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}}}f(x,\theta,N,\mathrm{loc})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>loc</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>loc</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}}}f(x,\theta,N,\mathrm{loc})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E9Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E9Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{0}}f(x,\theta,0,\varnothing)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{0}}f(x,\theta,0,\varnothing).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem.<a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Monotonic Bound on Performance) ‣ III-C Parameter spaces and function properties ‣ III The SimE framework via vision-language models with adapters ‣ A Simple Efficiency Incremental Learning Framework via Vision-Language Model with Nonlinear Multi-Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> tells us that, as we increase adapter number from <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and further to <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, we expand the parameter space and thus cannot lower the optimal performance. In practice, we expect the improvement of number of adapters could leverage this extra capacity, but no guarantee is given
on whether the final solution <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is indeed close to the supremum.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Non-monotonic Actual Solutions)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="loc" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">loc</annotation></semantics></math> be a specific insertion strategy (AdaptMLP, AdapterAtten,AdapterAll).
Then for <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;N</annotation></semantics></math>, it is possible that</span></p>
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{M,\mathrm{loc}}}f(\theta)&gt;\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}}}f(\theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>loc</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">&gt;</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>loc</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{M,\mathrm{loc}}}f(\theta)&gt;\sup_{\theta\in\Theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}}}f(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">yet</span></p>
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\bigl(\theta_{M,\mathrm{loc}_{1}}^{*}\bigr)\;&lt;\;f\bigl(\theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}_{2}}^{*}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>loc</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>loc</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\bigl(\theta_{M,\mathrm{loc}_{1}}^{*}\bigr)\;&lt;\;f\bigl(\theta_{N,\mathrm{loc}_{2}}^{*}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">showing that simply increasing adapter connections (e.g., MLP+Atten in the same block) does not necessarily beat a smaller or different-located Adapter design.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem.<a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Non-monotonic Actual Solutions) ‣ III-C Parameter spaces and function properties ‣ III The SimE framework via vision-language models with adapters ‣ A Simple Efficiency Incremental Learning Framework via Vision-Language Model with Nonlinear Multi-Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> highlights a fundamental gap
between the theoretical capacity (Theorem.<a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Monotonic Bound on Performance) ‣ III-C Parameter spaces and function properties ‣ III The SimE framework via vision-language models with adapters ‣ A Simple Efficiency Incremental Learning Framework via Vision-Language Model with Nonlinear Multi-Adapters" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) and
the actual performance of he model. In particular, adding more Adapters in a single block (transition from Atten to MLP+Atten, etc.) expands the space
yet can fail to yield better performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<div id="S3.F3.3" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:103.5pt;"><img src="2603.11211v1/3.1.png" id="S3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:143/90;" width="143" height="90" alt="Refer to caption">
<p id="S3.F3.3.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.F3.3.1.1" class="ltx_text">(a)</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<div id="S3.F3.4" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:103.5pt;"><img src="2603.11211v1/3.2.png" id="S3.F3.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:143/90;" width="143" height="90" alt="Refer to caption">
<p id="S3.F3.4.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.F3.4.1.1" class="ltx_text">(b)</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<div id="S3.F3.5" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:103.5pt;"><img src="2603.11211v1/3.3.png" id="S3.F3.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:143/90;" width="143" height="90" alt="Refer to caption">
<p id="S3.F3.5.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.F3.5.1.1" class="ltx_text">(c)</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<div id="S3.F3.6" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:103.5pt;"><img src="2603.11211v1/3.4.png" id="S3.F3.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:143/90;" width="143" height="90" alt="Refer to caption">
<p id="S3.F3.6.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.F3.6.1.1" class="ltx_text">(d)</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<div id="S3.F3.7" class="ltx_block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:103.5pt;"><img src="2603.11211v1/3.5.png" id="S3.F3.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:143/91;" width="143" height="91" alt="Refer to caption">
<p id="S3.F3.7.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center"><span id="S3.F3.7.1.1" class="ltx_text">(e)</span></p>
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
