<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A0.T8.9" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">TABLE VIII</span>: </span><span id="A0.T8.10" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:129%;">Last accuracy of different CIL methods on CIFAR100. The accuracy of Task <math id="A0.T8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A0.T8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,2,\ldots,10\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,2,\ldots,10\}</annotation></semantics></math> reported here is the last accuracy over all the previous tasks (i.e., Tasks <math id="A0.T8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,2,\ldots,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,2,\ldots,t</annotation></semantics></math>). If not otherwise specified, the method uses ResNet as the backbone, where <math id="A0.T8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\dagger}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\dagger}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the result based on the CLIP ViT-L/14 pre-trained on Laion-2B. The best results are coloured grey.</span></figcaption>
