<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A0.F7.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 7</span>: </span><span id="A0.F7.8" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Avg accuracy and Last accuracy of every Task on CIFAR100 and TinyImageNet with CLIP ViT-B/16. The Last accuracy of Task <math id="A0.F7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A0.F7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\{1,2,...,20\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.110em" minsize="1.110em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\{1,2,...,20\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Top-1 accuracy over all the previous Tasks (i.e., Task <math id="A0.F7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1,2,...,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1,2,...,t</annotation></semantics></math>). and the Avg accuracy is the average value of Last accuracy over all the previous Tasks. The 100 classes of TinyImageNet are used as base classes.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A0.T9" class="ltx_table">
